  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alabama received $260M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 98.7% year over year. Award count totaled 589, and average award size was $441K. Fiscal trends show large prior-year totals: FY22 obligations were $15B, FY23 obligations were $16.5B, FY24 obligations were $19.1B, FY25 obligations were $20.6B, and FY26 obligations were $20.2B. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration led buyers with $132M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $87.1M and the Department of Justice with $27.3M. THE BOEING COMPANY received $91M, AMERESCO INC received $52.3M, and NAPHCARE LLC received $21.9M. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $91M, and Engineering Services accounted for $64.1M. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals that are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations much lower than prior years?",
        "body": "The FY2027 total obligations are $260M, a large drop from prior fiscal years that reached as high as $20.6B in FY25. Obligations fell 98.7% year over year. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, which explains the gap versus full-year totals from FY22 through FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Alabama federal contracting so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $132M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $87.1M, together accounting for the bulk of FY2027 obligations. THE BOEING COMPANY received $91M and AMERESCO INC received $52.3M, while Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $91M and Engineering Services accounted for $64.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
